Check the supplied text against `.agents/rules/documentation-standards.md` for clear language-standard violations only.

Flag only clearly non-Japanese prose in a place that requires Japanese, or low-level C++/Python implementation details used as the conceptual specification itself (for example, exposing `bytearray` or raw struct pointers as the design concept).

Do not flag English code/API identifiers, registered metadata keywords, test IDs, Mermaid tokens, or terms whose English spelling is required by an external standard. Do not judge stylistic preference, sentence length, or a phrase as defective merely because it could be rewritten more elegantly. Obvious typos and missing text are handled by the dedicated typo/omission check. If the language is understandable and the English text is an allowed identifier or formal term, answer that no violation is present.
